<title>FINLAND: MERITA FALLS ON PRE-H1 PROFIT-TAKING.</title>
<headline>MERITA FALLS ON PRE-H1 PROFIT-TAKING.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish banking group Merita Oy fell on Monday on profit-taking ahead of its H1 results due on Wednesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1605/1305 GMT, Merita traded at 22.80 markka, down 0.70 markka or 2.98 percent in moderate 19 million markka turnover.</p>
<p>One broker said no investor seemed to be selling big stakes.</p>
<p>&quot;It will trade around 23.00 markka until Wednesday, it will not pick up before that,&quot; another broker said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 248</p>
